 "name": "task-871a8809-panel-lane-crossings",
 "old_string": "- Avoid the rejected overfill: do not infer a color lane merely because it has a single marker in a panel row/column. Require alignment supported by at least two markers of that color; then extend that lane. In the accepted test, the color-2 marker at panel (3,0) was supported by the other color-2 marker at (1,0) to define the vertical lane.",
 "new_string": "- **Critical correction from the rejected first attempt:** Lane orientation is determined by the aligned marker positions, not by the count of markers along one panel row or column. In the accepted 28x28 test, color-3 markers at panels (0,2) and (4,2) were vertically aligned, so they formed a vertical color-3 lane through every panel of column 2 (including row 1). The first attempt incorrectly filled panel row 0 with color 3 merely because it contained one marker, and also incorrectly extended color 3 into panel row 2. The second attempt, using the end-marker alignment and resulting cross, was accepted. Likewise, color-2 markers at panel row 1, columns 0 and 4 define a horizontal lane; markers at panel rows 1 and 3, column 0 define a vertical lane. Require at least two same-color marker panels aligned on a common panel row/column, and extend only that lane."
